WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.740
An artificial synapse detected early prostate cancer with perfect accuracy in a blind test of 105 patients by reading DNA markers. This is Planetterrian Daily, episode 146. The device identified every early case among the full set of patients. It processes epigenetic markers through a neuron-like process that bypasses full sequencing steps. Researchers see potential for rapid, low-cost screening of other cancers using the same

00:00:29.740 --> 00:00:48.000
approach. Follow-up work will test performance across larger and more diverse cohorts. Now shifting to infection effects on brain structure. MRI scans revealed alterations in regions tied to memory, emotion, and executive function after confirmed COVID-19 infection.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:01:00.820
The changes appeared in patients scanned following infection with some pre and post-infection comparisons available. Researchers compared the imaging data to map the extent of structural and functional shifts.

00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:17.420
The pattern helps explain persistent neurological symptoms reported by many recovered individuals. Additional cohorts will clarify duration and reversibility of the changes. On a different note, recent exercise data point to higher volumes for protection.

00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:36.380
A large observational study found that the standard 150 minutes of moderate to vigorous activity conferred only modest risk reduction. Benefits increased markedly at 560 to 610 minutes per week. Activity types included brisk walking, running, and cycling.

00:01:36.380 --> 00:01:56.600
The dose response curve was derived from health records of hundreds of thousands of participants. Longer term follow-up will test whether the pattern holds for specific cardiac events. Most people assume that spending time alone automatically produces loneliness, and that simply adding social contact will fix it.

00:01:56.600 --> 00:02:10.480
The distinction is more biological than that. Right now your brain maintains separate maps, one tracking the number of interactions you have, and another registering whether those interactions meet an internal expectation of connection.

00:02:11.320 --> 00:02:18.400
When the second map signals a mismatch, stress hormones, and inflammatory pathways rise even if your calendar is full.

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:29.320
One memorable figure comes from population studies showing that the mortality risk tied to loneliness persists after statistical control for actual contact frequency.

00:02:29.800 --> 00:02:40.680
The next time you notice persistent fatigue or low mood, despite regular social activity, consider whether the quality of connection not the quantity is the variable worth adjusting.

00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:50.560
Now moving to gratitude research across many countries, more than 10,000 participants across 34 countries completed one of several gratitude prompts.

00:02:51.340 --> 00:03:03.760
The study measured changes in affect relationship quality and reciprocity. Results published in PNAS identify which exercises produce the largest effects in different cultural settings.

00:03:03.760 --> 00:03:12.580
Resilient researchers contributed data from 598 online participants, shifting focus to dietary sweetness trials.

00:03:13.300 --> 00:03:24.720
In a six month randomized trial participants assigned to high-low or average sweetness diets showed no group differences in preference, body weight, or diabetes, and heart disease risk markers.

00:03:25.720 --> 00:03:38.180
Many returned to prior habits after the intervention ended. The study measured intake cravings and biomarkers at multiple time points. Results challenge assumptions that sweetness exposure drives long-term preference.

00:03:38.820 --> 00:03:51.040
Turning to reproductive health observations. Analysis of 10,338 births found equivalent median birth weights and pre-term delivery rates between vegan and unrestricted diet mothers.

00:03:52.040 --> 00:03:59.380
Vegan mothers had lower average BMI but no increase in anemia transfusions gestational diabetes or hypertension.

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:10.620
The observational data set controlled for key demographic and clinical variables. Larger prospective studies are needed to examine micronutrient status in greater detail.

00:04:11.300 --> 00:04:18.760
A weekly summary segment notes recurring threads around sensor and imaging tools refining early detection across diseases.

00:04:19.760 --> 00:04:32.440
Parallel threads on meta-google and cohere have explored how large-scale AI models accelerate genome design and protein structure work with results now moving from proof of concept into applied biology questions.

00:04:32.820 --> 00:04:38.940
These threads continue to intersect with recent findings on brain changes and behavioral interventions.

00:04:38.940 --> 00:04:50.740
Next up, bird song research shows structural features shared with human language. The study compared sequential patterns and combinatorial rules in bird song to spoken language.

00:04:51.460 --> 00:05:02.800
Researchers documented recurring motifs and hierarchical organization in multiple song bird species. The findings suggest convergent evolution of complex vocal communication.

00:05:02.800 --> 00:05:11.860
Data came from field recordings and statistical modeling of syllable transitions. Butterfly range data now from a global compilation.

00:05:12.560 --> 00:05:24.640
Researchers compiled records for 1,758 species representing 10% of known butterflies. 80% showed range expansions and 27% showed contractions.

00:05:24.640 --> 00:05:36.180
79% of shifts aligned with climate change or extreme weather. 22% of species changed elevation with the data set published in nature ecology and evolution.

00:05:36.980 --> 00:05:48.660
On another front, winter canola added to corn soy rotations shows modeled benefits. University of Illinois simulations modeled Midwest farm economics and environmental outcomes.

00:05:48.660 --> 00:06:00.900
Adding winter canola increased annual returns while reducing erosion and nutrient loss. The crop fits existing equipment and harvest windows with model runs across multiple soil types.

00:06:01.600 --> 00:06:10.760
Field trials are planned to validate the projections. Dodo cognition appears higher than historical accounts suggested based on new anatomical work.

00:06:10.760 --> 00:06:19.460
New analysis of skull endocasts and comparative neuroanatomy revised earlier estimates of brain size relative to body mass.

00:06:20.020 --> 00:06:30.640
The work places the extinct bird cognition closer to other pigeons than to the stupid stereotype. Mauritius fossil and historical records supplied the anatomical data.

00:06:30.640 --> 00:06:42.680
Reduced gravity shifts human movement patterns in measurable ways. Texas A&amp;M experiments used NASA supported reduced gravity environments to measure reaching and manipulation tasks.

00:06:43.480 --> 00:06:57.460
Participants adopted straighter less variable trajectories when gravitational cues diminished. The work tracks how the nervous system recalibrates motor commands with data collection continuing across phases of simulated microgravity.

00:06:57.460 --> 00:07:09.240
Genome-wide study in rats maps low-key tied to a version-based learning. Over 1000 heterogeneous stock rats completed runway progressive ratio and punishment tasks.

00:07:09.840 --> 00:07:26.480
Significant low-key appeared on chromosomes 2356 and X. Candidate genes include several previously linked to human smoking initiation and neuronal cilia function with heritability estimates reaching 0.307 for some phenotypes.

00:07:26.480 --> 00:07:37.620
Early life stress leaves lasting epigenetic marks according to mouse experiments. Juvenile stress altered chromatin accessibility in ventral tegmental area neurons.

00:07:38.420 --> 00:07:52.340
The changes persisted into adulthood and affected stress response gene expression. Researchers mapped loosened DNA regions around key regulatory sequences linking early experience to long-term circuit sensitivity.

00:07:52.340 --> 00:08:07.500
Gut cell turnover rate tracks cell fluid content rather than specific nutrients in fruit flywork at the ricon center. Low nutrient conditions made gut cell interiors more watery triggering the turnover response.

00:08:08.260 --> 00:08:15.020
Researchers led by SOCANU found the mechanism operates independently of individual macro nutrients.

00:08:16.020 --> 00:08:29.820
Finding suggests gut epithelium senses hydration state as a proxy for food availability. Before we go keep an eye on expanded validation trials for the artificial synapse detector as larger cohorts report results.

00:08:30.360 --> 00:08:36.160
That covers today's science and health news. Share this with someone who's curious about the latest research.

